  "description": "Prunus cerasifera, felled to ground and stump ground out. (1)\r\n\r\n2x Norway Maple (Acer plamtnoides), self set, felled to ground and stump ground out. (2,3)\r\n\r\nFraxinus Excelsior, self set, felled to ground and stump ground out (4)\r\n\r\nLaurus nobilis, felled to ground and stump ground out. (5)\r\n\r\nThe removal of the Cherry would be due to its proximity to the water barrier and its been badly pruned before, further development of property to include planting another in the garden in a more suitable place.\r\n\r\nRemoval of two self set maples, due to their tall thin habit, they are competing with a very well established copper beech and their removal would allow the copper beech to fully express itself and have a unrestricted view of that tree from the house.\r\n\r\nRemoval of self set Ash tree which has grow tall and thin due to competition with copper beech. its removal will allow unrestricted view of copper beech from the far back of the river.\r\n\r\nRemoval of bay tree due to its size and position. its removal will allow unrestricted view of the copper beech and lime tree from the house and the far bank of the river.\r\n\r\nFurther plans to plant native trees in the garden to compliment the beech and the lime, these include, willow tree, cherry tree, a further copper beech and a silver birch.",
